<node id="1198519" title="Re^2: Which &quot;use&quot; statements in a module do &quot;bubble up&quot; to the callers? [SOLVED]" created="2017-09-01 10:34:52" updated="2017-09-01 10:34:52" _doctext_mode="lenient"><type id="11">note</type>
<author id="961">Anonymous Monk</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;tt&gt;[doc://use]&lt;/tt&gt; is &lt;tt&gt;require&lt;/tt&gt; followed by &lt;tt&gt;import&lt;/tt&gt;, no more and no less. &lt;tt&gt;import&lt;/tt&gt; is defined by the module in question, and can do &lt;i&gt;whatever it wants.&lt;/i&gt; Normally, it adds stuff to the caller's symbol table, but it doesn't have to.</doctext>
